.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NQKSADD 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqksadd ,
.Nm nqkslist ,
.Nm nqksget ,
.Nm nqkscert ,
.Nm nqkscput ,
.Nm nqkstrust ,
.Nm nqksdel ,
.Nm nqksexp ,
.Nm nqksimp ,
.Nm nqksurl
.Nd a store of other people's keys, their certifications and trust
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqksadd "const char *dir" "int kem" "int alg" "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen" "const char *name" "const char *email" "const char *card" "size_t cardlen" "uint8_t fp[32]"
.Ft int
.Fn nqkslist "const char *dir" "const char *q" "nqkse *e" "size_t cap" "size_t *n"
.Ft int
.Fn nqksget "const char *dir" "const uint8_t fp[32]" "int *kem" "int *alg" "uint8_t *pk" "size_t cap" "size_t *pklen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqkscert "const char *dir" "nqsalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen" "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen" "const uint8_t fp[32]" "int64_t at" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqkscput "const char *dir" "const char *cert" "size_t n"
.Ft int
.Fn nqkstrust "const char *dir" "const uint8_t fp[32]" "int level"
.Ft int
.Fn nqksdel "const char *dir" "const uint8_t fp[32]"
.Ft int
.Fn nqksexp "const char *dir" "const uint8_t fp[32]" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqksimp "const char *dir" "const char *bundle" "size_t n" "const char *email" "uint8_t fp[32]" "size_t *nkeys"
.Ft int
.Fn nqksurl "const char *email" "char *url" "size_t cap"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A key store is a folder,
.Fa dir ,
of other people's public keys.
For each key it holds the name and e-mail address of its holder, the
certifications other keys made of that, and the trust the owner of the
store places in the holder to certify.
A key is named by its fingerprint, the SHA-256 of the public key.
The folder must exist.
.Pp
.Fn nqksadd
puts in the key
.Fa pk
of the algorithm
.Fa alg ,
an
.Vt nqkalg
when
.Fa kem
is 1 and an
.Vt nqsalg
when it is 0.
Who holds it is said either by
.Fa card ,
an identity card
.Pq Xr nqcard 3
of
.Fa cardlen
bytes that must verify and name this key
.Po
.Fa name
and
.Fa email
are then
.Dv NULL
.Pc ,
or by
.Fa name
(1 to 255 bytes, as
.Xr nqcard 3
takes one) and
.Fa email
or
.Dv NULL .
A card is only for a signature key
.Fa ( kem
0) of the card's own algorithm
.Po
another is
.Er NQEARG
or
.Er NQEVRFY
.Pc ,
and is kept with the key.
A key that is there keeps its trust and takes the new name;
certifications of the old name no longer count.
.Fa fp ,
when not
.Dv NULL ,
gets the fingerprint.
.Pp
.Fn nqkslist
gives the entries, in the order of their fingerprints, that answer
.Fa q :
all of them when
.Fa q
is
.Dv NULL ,
else those whose fingerprint in hex starts with
.Fa q
(8 to 64 digits, of either case) or whose name, address or algorithm
name holds
.Fa q ,
ASCII letters of either case alike; an empty
.Fa q
is
.Er NQEARG .
.Fa n
gets their number, also when
.Fa e ,
of
.Fa cap
entries, holds fewer
.Pq Dv NQEBUF .
An entry is:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef struct {
  int kem;         /* 1: a KEM key, 0: a signature key */
  int alg;         /* nqkalg or nqsalg */
  uint8_t fp[32];
  size_t pklen;
  char name[256];
  char email[255]; /* "" when it has none */
  int card;        /* 1 when the store holds its card */
  int trust;       /* NQKTUNK ... NQKTULT */
  int valid;       /* NQKVNONE, NQKVMARG, NQKVFULL */
  size_t ncert;    /* certifications under its present name */
} nqkse;
.Ed
.Pp
.Fn nqksget
gives the key of fingerprint
.Fa fp .
.Pp
.Fn nqkscert
certifies the key
.Fa fp
of the store with the key pair
.Fa sk ,
.Fa pk
of the signature algorithm
.Fa alg
at the time
.Fa at
(seconds since 1970, UTC): a
.Ql noqtis-cert-1
statement in canonical JSON, signed under the context
.Ql noqtis-cert-1 ,
that the key belongs to the name and address the store has for it.
In symbols, with HEX the lower-case hex of a SHA-256 fingerprint, T the
time as
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ ,
and JCS the canonical JSON of RFC 8785:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
body = JCS({"alg": name of alg, "created": T, "email": email,
            "format": "noqtis-cert-1", "issuer": HEX(SHA-256(pk)),
            "key": HEX(fp), "keyalg": name of the key's algorithm,
            "name": name})
cert = JCS(body's members and "signature": B64(Sign(sk, body,
           "noqtis-cert-1")))
.Ed
.Pp
with Sign
.Xr nqsign 3 ,
pure and hedged, B64 the padded base64 of RFC 4648 section 4, and
email the empty string for a key with no address.
The key that certifies need not be in the store.
It is kept in the store and, when
.Fa out
is not
.Dv NULL ,
given out; when
.Fa cap
is too small nothing is kept,
.Fa *outlen
gets its size, and the call returns
.Er NQEBUF .
.Fn nqkscput
puts in a certification made elsewhere: the key it is about and the key
that made it must be in the store, the first under the name and address
it says, and its signature must verify.
.Pp
.Fn nqkstrust
sets a key's trust to
.Fa level :
.Dv NQKTUNK ,
.Dv NQKTNEVER ,
.Dv NQKTMARG ,
.Dv NQKTFULL
or
.Dv NQKTULT ,
the last for the owner's own keys.
.Fn nqksdel
removes a key, its card, and every certification of it and by it.
.Pp
A bundle is text to publish or send: the identity card of a signature
key, then every other key of the store that this key certified under
its own name and address, each with that certification, armored
.Pq Xr nqarmenc 3
under the labels
.Ql NOQTIS IDENTITY CARD ,
.Ql NOQTIS PUBLIC KEY
and
.Ql NOQTIS CERTIFICATION .
.Fn nqksexp
writes the bundle of the key
.Fa fp ,
which must have its card in the store.
.Fn nqksimp
reads one, of at most 1 MiB: the card must verify, every key after it
must come with a certification by the card's key that verifies and says
the card's name and address, and all of them go into the store.
.Fa fp ,
when not
.Dv NULL ,
gets the card key's fingerprint (on success only) and
.Fa nkeys
the number of keys put in, the card's own counted, also on an error,
for those before it.
With
.Fa email
not
.Dv NULL
the card must be for that address, ASCII letters of either case alike
.Pq Dv NQEVRFY .
Nothing a bundle brings is trusted or valid for that alone.
.Pp
.Fn nqksurl
gives the address a bundle is published at for an e-mail address:
.Ql https://<domain>/.well-known/noqtis/<hash> ,
the hash being the first 20 bytes, in hex (40 digits), of the SHA-256
of the part before the
.Ql @
with its ASCII letters in lower case, and the domain written in lower
case; a domain of other characters than letters, digits, dots and
hyphens is
.Er NQEARG .
Fetching it is the caller's.
.Pp
Validity follows from trust and certifications.
A key is fully valid
.Pq Dv NQKVFULL
when its trust is
.Dv NQKTULT ,
or when one fully valid key of trust
.Dv NQKTFULL
or more certified it, or three of trust
.Dv NQKTMARG ;
one or two marginal ones make it marginally valid
.Pq Dv NQKVMARG .
Certifications are followed five levels from an
.Dv NQKTULT
key; only signature keys certify, and not themselves.
.Pp
The folder is the owner's own state and is not signed.
A card, a certification and a key's fingerprint are checked when they
are put in; whoever can write the folder decides what it trusts.
A key's file there, named by the 64 hex digits of its fingerprint and
.Pa .pub ,
is a key file as
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1
writes one.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK
on success.
.Dv NQEARG
for a
.Dv NULL
pointer, a name or address out of the limits of
.Xr nqcard 3 ,
a key of the wrong length, a level that is not one, or a key pair that
does not match;
.Dv NQENOSUP
for an algorithm this noqtis does not know, and for Ed25519 alone as
the certifying key;
.Dv NQEIO
when the folder or a key's files cannot be read or written, a key that
is not there among them;
.Dv NQEDEC
for a file of the store, a card or a certification that is not one;
.Dv NQEVRFY
for a card or a certification whose signature does not verify, or that
names another key, name or address;
.Dv NQEBUF
for an output that is too small;
.Dv NQELIM ,
.Dv NQEMEM .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uint8_t fp[32];
nqkse e[8];
size_t n;

nqksadd(dir, 0, NQMLDSA65, ben, benlen, "Ben Example",
        "ben@example.org", NULL, 0, fp);
nqkscert(dir, NQMLDSA65, sk, sklen, pk, pklen, fp, time(NULL),
         NULL, 0, NULL);
nqkslist(dir, "ben", e, 8, &n);   /* e[0].valid, once my key is
                                     trusted ultimately: NQKVFULL */
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-keys 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqcard 3 ,
.Xr nqerr 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
.%A A. Rundgren
.%A B. Jordan
.%A S. Erdtman
.%T JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS)
.%R RFC 8785
.%D June 2020
.Re
